Learning Ansible – Core Components Simplified
 #Ansible #RHCE #Linux #Automation #LearningJourney
As I revise Ansible for my RHCE, I’m breaking down its core components to keep things clear and simple.
🔹 1. Control Node
 The main machine where Ansible is installed and commands are run from.
🔹 2. Managed Nodes
 The client systems (Linux machines) that Ansible connects to via SSH to execute tasks.
🔹 3. Inventory
 A file (like hosts) listing the IPs or hostnames of all managed nodes.
🔹 4. Modules
 Pre-built units of work – like yum, service, or copy – used inside playbooks to perform actions.
🔹 5. Playbook
 A .yml file where tasks are written in human-readable YAML format. These define what to do on each system.
🔹 6. Tasks
 Individual instructions inside a playbook. Example: Install a package, start a service, create a file.
🔹 7. Roles
 Structured way to organize playbooks and files for reusability and scalability.
Understanding these basics makes writing and organizing automation easier!


